= Homomorphism kernel examples
#tags("lie-theory")

- $frak("sl")(n, bb(C))$ is an ideal in $frak("gl")(n, bb(C))$
  because it's the kernel of homomorphism $"Tr" : bb(C)^(n times n) -> bb(C)^+$.

- $frak("sp")(1) times {0}$ is an ideal of $frak("so")(4)$
  because it's the kernel of homomorphism $phi : frak("sp")(1) times frak("sp")(1) -> frak("so")(4)$
  given by $(X, Y) mapsto (0, Y)$.

#cite("stillwell2008")[§6.3]
